# Build Waitlist

When the user says **"build the waitlist"** (with or without a spec file):

1. Read `.cursor/WAITLIST-BUILD.md` — master playbook
2. Read the user's spec in `.cursor/spec/*.md` (exclude `waitlist-spec.template.md` unless that's all they provided)
3. Follow templates in `.cursor/templates/` for design, architecture, sections, plumbing
4. Use this repo as the reference implementation for component patterns

## Defaults

- Standalone Next.js app at **repo root** (not `temp/`)
- Dark slate + emerald accent (override per spec)
- All copy in `lib/copy.ts`
- Web3Forms + Resend waitlist plumbing (standard)
- Generate `.cursor/rules/product-landing-handoff/` for future product app
- Tag `design-v1` after first successful build
- Never start/stop dev server

## This is validation only

Do not build product features. The real app is a separate repo that will borrow this design later (see `.cursor/templates/product-handoff.md`).
